cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "MazeRunner: A Continuous-Control Benchmark for Multimodal Models"
message: "If you use MazeRunner, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kenstler
    given-names: Bradley
license: MIT
version: 2.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-02
abstract: >
  MazeRunner evaluates whether multimodal models can perceive a rendered maze
  and execute one continuous drag trajectory through it, scored by swept-disk
  collision against the mask that stenciled the render. Version 2 is a
  difficulty ladder: 192 tasks over 8 topology families at 4 size levels plus
  warped twins of the 4 grid families, in 48 equally weighted cells; full
  traces released.
